---
source: crates/sentry-network/src/init.rs
expression: "format!(\"{text}\\n{}\", notes.join(\"\\n\"))"
---
# sentry's configuration: the networks sentry watches through their routers.
# Written by sentry: change it in the Config tab or with `sentry config`. Editing it
# in $EDITOR is fine, but comments are not kept: the next save writes it again
# from what it says, keeping the file before beside it (network_config.yaml.bak-<time>).

networks:
  home:
    router:
      ssh: myrouter
    expect:
      zones:
        dmz:
          - dmz
        lan:
          - lan
        wan:
          - wan
          - wan6
      forwards:
        - name: web-https
          port: 443
          to: "203.0.113.10"
        - name: game it's
          proto: any
          port: 8000-8010
          to: "192.0.2.20"
    devices:
      - mac: 00:00:5e:00:53:10
        hostname: nas
      - mac: 00:00:5e:00:53:11
      - hostname: my-phone
        private_mac: true
    maintenance:
      items:
        - id: firmware
          kind: firmware
        - id: packages
          kind: packages
        - id: backup
          kind: backup

· networks.home.router: Example Router AX · OpenWrt 25.12.3 · mediatek/filogic
· networks.home.router: its ports and radios now: eth1 (wan) 1G · lan1 (lan) 1G · lan2 (lan) 100M · lan3 (lan) no link · lan4 (dmz) 1G · phy0-ap0 (lan) · phy1-ap0 (lan)
· networks.home.expect: what the firewall looks like now, taken as what's expected.
· networks.home.expect.forwards: not taken: forward half: no port or no address to go to
· networks.home.devices[0]: holds 192.0.2.10 now
· networks.home.devices[1]: holds 192.0.2.11 now
· networks.home.devices[2]: holds 192.0.2.20 now
· networks.home.devices: every device holding a lease now. Give the ones you know a `name:` and delete the rest. `private_mac`: its MAC is locally administered, as a phone's private address is, so it's known by its hostname (give `mac:` instead if its MAC never changes).
· networks.home.devices: not listed: 1 with a private MAC and no hostname
· networks.home.backup.recipients: config backups are encrypted on this machine. Put a public recipient here (an age1… key; `sentry-network backup key <file>` makes one) to have them.
